loyment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"an OIDC provider, normally Keycloak, with a realm/tenant and client for Lamassu"},"205":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"Envoy Gateway 1.8+ and a `GatewayClass`"},"206":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"cert-manager 1.14+; for trusted TLS, either a trusted issuer or a Kubernetes TLS Secret"},"207":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"a StorageClass and an external traffic design"},"208":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"The chart defaults to a `GatewayClass` named `eg`. Change `gateway.className` if your platform team uses another name."},"209":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"You provide the PostgreSQL server. The chart's pre-install job connects with the supplied credentials, creates the required `pki`, `authz` and `wfx` databases and service schemas, runs migrations, and applies `services.authz.bootstrap`."},"210":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"The chart has no Helm dependencies that install PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ, an OIDC provider, Envoy Gateway or cert-manager."},"211":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Install or upgrade the Envoy Gateway CRDs before its controller. The commands below match the version used by the Lamassu Helm repository:"},"212":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Create the default `GatewayClass` if it does not already exist. Save this manifest as `gateway-class.yaml`:"},"213":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Install cert-manager separately before Lamassu. The current chart renders its self-signed issuer and CA certificate resources even when `tls.type: external` makes the Gateway use an existing TLS Secret. Selecting external TLS therefore does not remove the cert-manager prerequisite."},"214":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"Start with the chart defaults and override the environment-specific values. This example assumes PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ and Keycloak are reachable through Kubernetes DNS, and exposes Keycloak at `/auth` through the shared Lamassu Gateway:"},"215":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"Do not add `gateway.addresses` by default. Leave address assignment to the load-balancer implementation unless your network design requires a specific Kubernetes-side VIP. The public IP of an upstream NAT gateway or reverse proxy does not belong in this value."},"216":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"If Keycloak is external and already has its own reachable URL, point the OIDC settings at it and omit the `/auth` entry from `gateway.extraRouting`."},"217":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#tls-with-an-existing-secret","content":"Create a Secret containing `tls.crt` and `tls.key`, then reference it:"},"218":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"There is no implicit superuser. Create the role or group expected by `services.authz.bootstrap` in the OIDC provider and assign it to at least one administrator before exposing Lamassu."},"219":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"The pre-install and pre-upgrade job applies the bootstrap idempotently: existing principals are preserved and missing grants are added."},"220":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"Test both an authorized identity and a denied identity. If no token matches an active bootstrap principal, nobody can administer the PKI."},"221":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"See Access control for the principal and policy model."},"222":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#3-install-lamassu","content":"To install a local checkout instead:"},"223":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#4-verify-the-deployment","content":"The Gateway should report `PROGRAMMED=True`. If it is programmed but has no usable address, continue with Expose the Gateway."},"224":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#4-verify-the-deployment","content":"The Helm test checks the CA, DMS Manager, Device Manager and VA health endpoints and verifies the UI response."},"225":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"Before going live, review:"},"226":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"backup and recovery for PostgreSQL and persistent volumes"},"227":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"a production KMS engine; the default filesystem engine is not an HA design"},"228":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"shared VA storage before increasing VA replicas"},"229":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"managed OIDC roles and removal of evaluation credentials"},"230":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"a trusted TLS issuer or externally managed certificate"},"231":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"resource requests, replicas, autoscaling, disruption budgets and placement"},"232":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"SMTP, observability and alert delivery"},"233":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"follow Upgrade the Helm chart and the version notes in `charts/lamassu/CHANGELOG/` before every upgrade"},"234":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"The complete values reference is maintained in `charts/lamassu/VALUES.md` in the Helm repository."},"235":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","type":"page","content":"Upgrade the Helm chart","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Deployment","Kubernetes self-managed"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration"},"236":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","content":"Upgrade a Helm-managed Lamassu deployment, including the 3.8.0 to 4.0.0 chart migration and the KMS and VA persistent-data steps."},"237":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#upgrade-the-helm-chart","content":"Upgrade the Helm chart"},"238":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#what-changes-in-400","content":"What changes in 4.0.0"},"239":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#what-the-upgrade-job-does-automatically","content":"What the upgrade job does automatically"},"240":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#before-you-upgrade","content":"Before you upgrade"},"241":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#update-your-values-file","content":"Update your values file"},"242":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#run-the-upgrade","content":"Run the upgrade"},"243":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"Migrate the KMS and VA data"},"244":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#verify-the-migration","content":"Verify the migration"},"245":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#delete-the-old-volumes","content":"Delete the old volumes"},"246":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"247":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#related-pages","content":"Related pages"},"248":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#upgrade-the-helm-chart","content":"Use this guide to upgrade a Helm-managed deployment. It walks through the 3.8.0 to 4.0.0 chart migration in full: the values to review, the database changes the chart applies automatically and the manual steps for installations that keep KMS keys or VA CRLs on local volumes. Version-specific notes for other upgrades live in the `charts/lamassu/CHANGELOG/` directory of the `lamassu-helm` repository."},"249":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#upgrade-the-helm-chart","content":"If you are not upgrading an existing release, go straight to Install with Helm. The manual data steps on this page only apply to deployments upgraded from 3.8.x that use local KMS or VA storage."},"250":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#what-changes-in-400","content":"Version 4.0.0 is a security-hardening release. Three changes affect upgrades:"},"251":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#what-changes-in-400","content":"**Release-scoped resource names.** Every chart-managed resource is now named `<release>-lamassu-<component>`, for example `lamassu-kms`, instead of the fixed, unscoped names used in 3.8.0 (`kms`, `va`, `ca`, ...). With a release named `prod` the StatefulSets become `prod-lamassu-kms` and `prod-lamassu-va`, not `prod-kms`. The `nameOverride` and `fullnameOverride` values change the prefix."},"252":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#what-changes-in-400","content":"**Non-root containers.** Every workload runs as the numeric user `65532:65532` with a `RuntimeDefault` seccomp profile and dropped capabilities. Pods do not mount the service-account token by default, and the chart creates a dedicated ServiceAccount."},"253":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#what-changes-in-400","content":"**Strict values validation.** `values.schema.json` rejects unknown top-level keys, so leftover 3.8.0 blocks fail `helm lint` and `helm upgrade` outright instead of being silently ignored."},"254":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#what-changes-in-400","content":"`services.connectors` also becomes a map keyed by connector ID, and the chart no longer injects pod anti-affinity or topology spread rules."},"255":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#what-changes-in-400","content":"Kubernetes derives the PVC name from the StatefulSet pod name (`<volumeClaimTemplate>-<pod-name>`). Renaming the `kms` and `va` StatefulSets means `helm upgrade` binds brand-new, empty PVCs instead of the existing ones. Your KMS key material and VA CRLs are not deleted — the old PVCs are orphaned, not removed — but the upgraded pods fail to find them with `no such file or directory` (KMS) or `code=NotFound` (VA) until you move the data across yourself. All other renamed resources are stateless and are recreated without data-loss risk."},"256":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#what-the-upgrade-job-does-automatically","content":"Before any service starts, the chart's pre-install/pre-upgrade job prepares PostgreSQL:"},"257":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#what-the-upgrade-job-does-automatically","content":"Creates the `pki`, `authz` and `wfx` databases when they do not exist."},"258":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#what-the-upgrade-job-does-automatically","content":"Ensures one schema per service database (`alerts`, `ca`, `va`, `devicemanager`, `dmsmanager`, `kms`) inside the shared `pki` database, and folds 3.8.0's separate per-service databases into it, importing their data."},"259":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#what-the-upgrade-job-does-automatically","content":"Runs the database migrations for every schema."},"260":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#what-the-upgrade-job-does-automatically","content":"Migrates authz, preloads its policies and seeds the `services.authz.bootstrap` principals."},"261":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#what-the-upgrade-job-does-automatically","content":"The job is idempotent, so a failed upgrade can be retried. It requires a PostgreSQL role allowed to create databases and schemas, as described in Install with Helm."},"262":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#before-you-upgrade","content":"Record the names of your existing local-storage PVCs:"},"263":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#before-you-upgrade","content":"`helm upgrade` does not touch or delete the old PVCs, but nothing references them after the upgrade. You need their names to copy data and to clean up later; do not delete them until the new volumes are verified."},"264":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#before-you-upgrade","content":"Remove values the strict schema now rejects, for example the old `toolbox:` block. Update your values file lists every rename."},"265":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#update-your-values-file","content":"**Add `services.authz` (required).** 3.8.0 had no authorization service: every route accepted any valid token. 4.0.0 adds fine-grained, entity-level authorization, and a 3.8.0 values file has nothing to migrate *from* — you must add the configuration:"},"266":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#update-your-values-file","content":"`authz` is the authorization service's own storage for principals, grants and policies (`services.authz.database`, `authz` by default)."},"267":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#update-your-values-file","content":"`pki` is the database the authorization engine queries when it evaluates policies against entities such as CAs, certificates, devices, DMSs, KMS keys and VA roles."},"268":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#update-your-values-file","content":"Only the `database` field of each credentials entry is read. Connection settings always come from the global `postgres.hostname`, `postgres.port`, `postgres.username` and `postgres.password` values."},"269":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#update-your-values-file","content":"Confirm `services.authz.bootstrap` (present by default in the chart) matches how your OIDC provider assigns the `pki-admin` realm role. Without a principal that matches the bootstrap rule, nobody can administer the PKI — there is no implicit superuser."},"270":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#update-your-values-file","content":"**Rename `toolbox` to `connectivityTest`.** The `helm test` connectivity hook now uses the upstream-maintained `curlimages/curl` image pinned by digest instead of the chart-owned toolbox image:"},"271":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#update-your-values-file","content":"**Remove per-service identity overrides.** `services.kms.securityContext.runAsGroup: 0` and `services.authz.securityContext.runAsUser`/`runAsGroup: 999` no longer exist. Every service runs under the chart-wide `65532:65532`, and KMS volume and PKCS#11 socket group access is handled automatically by the pod-level `fsGroup: 65532`."},"272":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#update-your-values-file","content":"**Convert `services.connectors` to a map.** Each entry is keyed by its stable connector ID and declares `type` and `image`:"},"273":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#update-your-values-file","content":"**Check the TLS issuer values.** With `tls.certManagerOptions.issuer` empty (the default), the chart creates a self-signed, release-scoped issuer — for example `lamassu-downstream-ca-selfsigned-issuer` with release `lamassu`. The legacy literal `downstream-ca-selfsigned-issuer` from 3.8.0-era values is still accepted and resolves to the same release-scoped issuer; point `tls.certManagerOptions.clusterIssuer` at your own issuer for corporate TLS."},"274":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#update-your-values-file","content":"**Review scheduling and ports.** The chart no longer injects pod anti-affinity or topology spread constraints — configure `affinity` and `topologySpreadConstraints` explicitly where your cluster needs them. The `services.ui.port` default is now `8085`, the unprivileged chart-wide port of the rootless image, so update overrides that pinned `80`. The shared `probes:` block is replaced by independent `livenessProbe`, `readinessProbe` and `startupProbe` blocks."},"275":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#run-the-upgrade","content":"Helm runs the database job before applying any workload, so services never start against an unprepared database. If validation rejects unknown values, fix the values file and re-run."},"276":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"Skip this section on fresh installs, or when `services.kms.cryptoEngines` never used a `filesystem` engine and `services.va.fileStore.type` was never `local`."},"277":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"**Find the new StatefulSets and PVCs.** Their names depend on the release name and any `nameOverride`/`fullnameOverride`; the PVC name is `<volumeClaimTemplate>-<StatefulSet name>-0`:"},"278":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"With release `lamassu` and the default chart name, the new PVCs are `golang-engine-storage-lamassu-kms-0` and `local-crl-file-storage-lamassu-va-0`; with release `prod` they are `golang-engine-storage-prod-lamassu-kms-0` and `local-crl-file-storage-prod-lamassu-va-0`. Confirm both old and new PVCs exist before continuing."},"279":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"**Scale the new StatefulSets down** so nothing writes to either volume while you copy:"},"280":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"**Run a short-lived helper pod** that mounts all four claims:"},"281":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"**Inspect before writing** so you do not clobber data the new pods may already have written:"},"282":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"An empty result is the common case: a StatefulSet's own pod rarely gets far enough to write anything when its dependent data is missing."},"283":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"**Copy the data and align ownership**:"},"284":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"The `chown` is required even if the old files already look non-root-owned. 3.8.0 did not pin a container identity, so files could carry any image-declared UID; 4.0.0 requires exactly `65532:65532` and does not fall back to whatever the image declares."},"285":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#migrate-the-kms-and-va-data","content":"**Scale back up and remove the helper**:"},"286":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#verify-the-migration","content":"KMS and VA logs show no `no such file or directory` or `code=NotFound` errors."},"287":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#verify-the-migration","content":"A previously issued CRL is servable again: `GET /crl/<ca-ski>` on VA."},"288":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#verify-the-migration","content":"`helm test \"$RELEASE\" -n $NAMESPACE --logs` passes; the connectivity hook checks the CA, DMS Manager, Device Manager and VA health endpoints and the UI response."},"289":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#verify-the-migration","content":"Sign in with an administrator identity and confirm operations are authorized."},"290":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#delete-the-old-volumes","content":"Only once everything works, delete the orphaned 3.8.0 volumes to reclaim storage:"},"291":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#troubleshooting","content":"**KMS or VA pods crash with `no such file or directory` or `code=NotFound` right after the upgrade.** The new pods are bound to the new empty PVCs and the data migration has not run yet, or was copied into the wrong PVC. Follow Migrate the KMS and VA data and check that all four claims exist."},"292":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#troubleshooting","content":"**`helm upgrade` fails with an unknown-key validation error.** Remove or rename the legacy values — typically the `toolbox:` block — because the strict schema rejects top-level keys it does not know."},"293":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#troubleshooting","content":"**The upgrade fails at the database job.** The PostgreSQL role cannot create databases or schemas; grant the required privileges, or create the `pki`, `authz` and `wfx` databases yourself, then re-run the upgrade."},"294":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#troubleshooting","content":"**Nobody can log in after the upgrade.** Check that `services.authz.bootstrap` matches a role your OIDC provider actually assigns (see Access control) and that the migration Job completed successfully."},"295":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#related-pages","content":"<Card title=\"Install with Helm\" description=\"Prepare dependencies, configure values and install a controlled deployment.\" href=\"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm\" />"},"296":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/migration#related-pages","content":"<Card title=\"Expose the Gateway\" description=\"Choose an external traffic design and handle Gateway addressing.\" href=\"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking\" />"},"297":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"page","content":"Expose the Gateway","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Deployment","Kubernetes self-managed"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking"},"298":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","content":"Choose how clients reach Lamassu, when to set gateway.addresses and how to design multiple Gateways."},"299":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#expose-the-lamassu-gateway","content":"Expose the Lamassu Gateway"},"300":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Do you need `gateway.addresses`?"},"301":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#recommended-single-node-design","content":"Recommended single-node design"},"302":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"K3s"},"303":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#bare-metal-with-metallb-or-kube-vip","content":"Bare metal with MetalLB or kube-vip"},"304":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#external-reverse-proxy-nat-or-vpn","content":"External reverse proxy, NAT or VPN"},"305":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"What if you need three Gateways?"},"306":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"Decision guide"},"307":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Verify the traffic path"},"308":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#expose-the-lamassu-gateway","content":"The Lamassu chart creates one shared Gateway with HTTP and HTTPS listeners. Envoy Gateway normally creates a dedicated proxy deployment and a `LoadBalancer` Service for it."},"309":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#expose-the-lamassu-gateway","content":"External reachability is the result of the whole path. A `Gateway` resource alone does not configure your router, firewall, DNS, cloud load balancer or upstream NAT."},"310":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Usually, no. If you omit it, the Gateway controller and the cluster load-balancer implementation can assign an address and report it in `Gateway.status.addresses` and the generated Service status."},"311":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Set it only when:"},"312":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"your cloud or bare-metal load balancer supports requesting a specific address"},"313":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"that address is allocated to this Gateway"},"314":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"the surrounding network already routes traffic for it to the cluster"},"315":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"This requests `192.168.1.50`; it does not claim the IP on your LAN or make it reachable."},"316":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Keep these two settings separate:"},"317":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"`gateway.addresses` requests an address for the Gateway."},"318":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"`tls.certManagerOptions.certSpec.addresses` adds IP subject alternative names to the TLS certificate."},"319":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"If users connect by DNS name, put that name in `tls.certManagerOptions.certSpec.hostnames`. Do not copy an upstream proxy's public IP into `gateway.addresses`."},"320":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#recommended-single-node-design","content":"For a small VM running K3s or MicroK8s, use one external Lamassu Gateway and route every Lamassu endpoint through it:"},"321":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#recommended-single-node-design","content":"This design uses one IP, one TLS entry point and one pair of ports. The chart already creates the required routes."},"322":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"K3s ServiceLB implements each `LoadBalancer` Service with pods that reserve the Service ports on the node. On a single node, only one Service can therefore own port 80 and one can own port 443. The default K3s Traefik Service may already hold both ports."},"323":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"For the recommended design:"},"324":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Use only one externally exposed Lamassu Gateway."},"325":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Ensure ports 80 and 443 are free. Disable or reconfigure Traefik if it is not part of your traffic path."},"326":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Allow those ports through the VM firewall and any upstream security group."},"327":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Point DNS at the VM's reachable address."},"328":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"See the K3s ServiceLB documentation for its host-port behavior and how to replace it with another load-balancer implementation."},"329":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#bare-metal-with-metallb-or-kube-vip","content":"Allocate a VIP from an address pool reachable on your LAN. You may request that VIP with `gateway.addresses` if the selected implementation supports it. Confirm the assigned address in status rather than assuming the request succeeded."},"330":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#external-reverse-proxy-nat-or-vpn","content":"An external public address can forward TCP 80 and 443 to the VM or to a Kubernetes-side VIP:"},"331":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#external-reverse-proxy-nat-or-vpn","content":"The public IP belongs to the external device. Leave `gateway.addresses` unset or set it to the actual Kubernetes-side address, never to an address that the cluster cannot bind."},"332":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"First decide whether you need three independent data planes or only three hostnames."},"333":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Requirement"},"334":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Recommended design"},"335":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Consequence"},"336":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Several Lamassu URLs or services"},"337":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"One Gateway with multiple routes"},"338":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"One IP and one proxy fleet; this is the chart default"},"339":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Independent Gateways and separate external IPs"},"340":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"One VIP per Gateway"},"341":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"All Gateways can use 80/443; requires a load balancer with an address pool"},"342":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Independent Gateways on one node and one IP"},"343":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Use different external ports"},"344":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Clients must include non-standard ports"},"345":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Separate TLS/mTLS termination behind one IP"},"346":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Front-door SNI routing to internal Gateways"},"347":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Advanced design; the front door uses TLS passthrough and each internal Gateway terminates its own TLS"},"348":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Separate Gateway resources but shared proxy infrastructure"},"349":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Envoy merged-Gateway mode"},"350":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Logical separation only; listeners must have unique port, protocol and hostname tuples"},"351":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Three independent `LoadBalancer` Services cannot all reserve the same node ports 80 and 443 through K3s ServiceLB. Use one shared Gateway, allocate distinct VIPs with another load-balancer implementation, or use different ports."},"352":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Envoy Gateway normally provisions a proxy fleet per `Gateway`. Its merged-Gateway mode can share one fleet and address, but it is not a drop-in switch for multiple Lamassu releases: the generated Lamassu listeners use the same ports and protocols without distinct hostnames, so they conflict unless you deliberately customize the listener design."},"353":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Use a front-door SNI design only when the internal Gateways must retain independent TLS or mTLS policy:"},"354":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"This requires distinct SNI hostnames and cluster networking outside the Lamassu chart."},"355":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If one Gateway can own TLS and routing, use the chart default."},"356":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If Gateways need independent policy and you can allocate IPs, use one VIP per Gateway."},"357":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If only the Kubernetes resources need separation, evaluate merged-Gateway mode and make every listener tuple unique."},"358":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If data planes and TLS termination must stay independent behind one IP, add a front-door SNI passthrough layer."},"359":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If none of those are possible, use different external ports or change the external network design."},"360":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Check, in order:"},"361":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"`Gateway` has `Accepted=True` and `Programmed=True`."},"362":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Its status contains the expected address."},"363":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"The generated `LoadBalancer` Service has a usable external address."},"364":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Port 443 reaches that address from the client network."},"365":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"DNS resolves to the externally reachable endpoint."},"366":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"The certificate contains the DNS name or IP used by the client."},"367":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"The Gateway API treats addresses as desired state that a controller may assign or reject; see the Gateway API overview for the resource model."},"368":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/deployment/self-hosted/overview","page_id":"/docs