m/pki/key-management-109","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Common Name (CN)**: main name of the identity."},"2184":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management-110","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Organization (O)**: organization or company."},"2185":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management-111","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Organizational Unit (OU)**: department or unit."},"2186":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management-112","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Country (C)**: two-letter country code."},"2187":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management-113","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**State / Province (ST)**: state or province."},"2188":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management-114","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Locality (L)**: city or locality."},"2189":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management-115","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Email Address**: contact email."},"2190":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management-116","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Subject Alternative Names (SANs)**: alternative names or identifiers, such as DNS or IP."},"2191":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management-117","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"Download the CSR and run `openssl req -in request.csr -noout -verify -text`. Check signature, subject and SAN before sending it. A CSR does not determine the final certificate by itself: issuance policy can replace its fields."},"2192":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management-118","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management#sign-locally-with-pkcs11","content":"Lamassu also offers specific help for local integrations through **Sign locally with OpenSSL & PKCS11 tools**."},"2193":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management-119","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management#sign-locally-with-pkcs11","content":"Requiere el módulo, token y permisos del proveedor correspondiente. Comprueba que el identificador de Lamassu se corresponde con el objeto accesible desde ese módulo. La configuración del módulo pertenece al entorno del cliente o al Despliegue."},"2194":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management-120","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/key-management#before-deleting-a-key","content":"Review **Related Entities** and locate CAs, certificates and validation processes that still need signatures. Revoking a CA does not remove the need to publish status during its retention period. Deleting a key does not automatically revoke its certificates either. Plan replacement and retention before using **Delete Key**; provider deletion behavior depends on the engine."},"2195":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"page","content":"Online validation with OCSP","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","PKI","Validation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp"},"2196":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","content":"Query signed status and verify the responder’s response."},"2197":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"How the responder works in Lamassu"},"2198":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#embedding-in-issued-certificates","content":"Embedding in issued certificates"},"2199":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"HTTP endpoints"},"2200":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"Generate and verify a query"},"2201":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#check-from-the-interface","content":"Check from the interface"},"2202":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"References"},"2203":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","content":"OCSP queries a certificate’s status and returns a signed response. This guide is for an integrator checking what Lamassu publishes and how the consumer must verify it. For complete identity validation, follow Certificate validation."},"2204":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"The responder retrieves the certificate by serial number and locates its issuing CA in the inventory. It translates persisted status as follows:"},"2205":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"Record status"},"2206":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"Signed response"},"2207":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"`ACTIVE`"},"2208":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"`Good`."},"2209":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"`REVOKED`"},"2210":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"`Revoked`, with revocation reason and timestamp."},"2211":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"Other states, including `INACTIVE` and `EXPIRED`"},"2212":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"`Unknown` if the certificate and issuer can be retrieved."},"2213":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"An absent serial number causes a lookup error; it does not guarantee a signed `Unknown` response. Lookup or signing errors produce an HTTP failure. Treat that as unavailable evidence according to consumer policy."},"2214":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"The issuing CA itself signs the response through its KMS-associated key. A delegated OCSP signing certificate is not used. An imported CA without a usable key cannot sign responses."},"2215":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"The implementation sets `thisUpdate` approximately one day before response generation and `nextUpdate` one day after: the declared window is about 48 hours. Inspect received values and apply your freshness policy. The response reflects stored status when queried; a previously cached copy does not change upon revocation."},"2216":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#embedding-in-issued-certificates","content":"The signer constructs OCSP URLs from configured VA domains and adds them to AIA. Without domains, there is no URL to add; an imported certificate retains its original extensions. Inspect the actual certificate:"},"2217":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#embedding-in-issued-certificates","content":"Check that the consumer can reach this URL. DNS, endpoint exposure and domain configuration belong to Deployment. Changing configuration does not modify already signed certificates."},"2218":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"The service accepts:"},"2219":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"Method"},"2220":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"VA service path"},"2221":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"Format"},"2222":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"`POST`"},"2223":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"`/ocsp`"},"2224":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"DER request, `Content-Type: application/ocsp-request`."},"2225":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"`GET`"},"2226":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"`/ocsp/{ocsp_request}`"},"2227":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"DER request encoded using padded URL Base64."},"2228":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"Use POST to avoid client encoding differences. A successful response has `Content-Type: application/ocsp-response` and a DER body. The public prefix depends on the Gateway; use the URL published in the certificate and checked by the operator."},"2229":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"You need OpenSSL 3.x, `device.crt`, its direct issuer’s certificate `issuer.pem` and the consumer’s trusted roots in `roots.pem`. For an intermediate issuer, also prepare `intermediates.pem` containing the intermediate CAs."},"2230":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"Generate the request:"},"2231":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"This example omits the nonce because the responder does not echo it. Verification relies on signature, response correspondence and timestamps; it does not demonstrate freshness through a nonce."},"2232":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"Replace the example URL with the inspected endpoint:"},"2233":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"Verify the returned DER:"},"2234":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"For intermediates, add `-verify_other intermediates.pem`. Require successful response verification and inspect the status corresponding to `device.crt`, issuer, serial, `thisUpdate` and `nextUpdate`. `Response verify OK` validates the response only: also observe `good`, `revoked` or `unknown`. Do not accept an identity based only on the command’s exit code."},"2235":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#check-from-the-interface","content":"**OCSP Check** shows what Lamassu returns for a selected certificate. Complete the check from the consumer’s network and trust store: a console query does not establish its validation configuration."},"2236":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#check-from-the-interface","content":"To check a change, save an earlier response, revoke a test certificate and request another response. The new query should reflect persisted status; compare timestamps to rule out reuse of an earlier response. If it fails, follow PKI troubleshooting."},"2237":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"RFC 6960: OCSP."},"2238":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"OpenSSL: openssl-ocsp."},"2239":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"<Card title=\"CRL service\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/crl\" />"},"2240":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"<Card title=\"Certificate validation\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/certificate-validation\" />"},"2241":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview","type":"page","content":"PKI","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","PKI"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview"},"2242":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview","content":"Administer keys and authorities, define issuance and verify the resulting certificates."},"2243":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview#start-here","content":"Start here"},"2244":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview#what-you-need","content":"What you need"},"2245":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview#core-capabilities","content":"Core capabilities"},"2246":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview#build-your-trust-hierarchy","content":"Build your trust hierarchy"},"2247":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview#protect-cryptographic-keys","content":"Protect cryptographic keys"},"2248":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview#issue-and-control-certificates","content":"Issue and control certificates"},"2249":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview#publish-validation-status","content":"Publish validation status"},"2250":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview#how-to-check-the-result","content":"How to check the result"},"2251":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview#continue","content":"Continue"},"2252":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview","content":"The PKI section explains how to build and operate X.509 trust in Lamassu: which authorities issue, which rules apply and how to check certificates. It is intended for PKI administrators and anyone who needs to use certificates in a consuming system."},"2253":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/overview#start-here","content":"Follow PKI getting started to create a CA, issue a client certificate and verify it with OpenSSL. The resul